    <md:uuid>647967de-6d2d-4001-98be-34ca074397e0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For numbers 1 – 9, use the following scenario:
  A car has a 16-gallon fuel tank. When driven on a highway, it has a gas mileage of 30 miles per gallon. The gas
  mileage (also called "fuel efficiency") tells us the number of miles the car can travel for a particular amount of
  fuel (one gallon of gasoline, in this case). After filling the gas tank, the driver got on a highway and drove for a
  while.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="c9c0b944-2eb3-43b2-acc4-79148148453b"><problem><para>
      <para>How many miles has the car traveled if it has 15 gallons left in the tank?
        </para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>30</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 30 miles. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
